SUMMARY:GPMS Class: Clay Witch Hat Tea Lights
DESCRIPTION:Bring on the spooky season! Join Elena in learning to make witch hat luminaries. Participants will create little witch hats to cover tea lights for another spooky cute Halloween decoration. The pieces will be dried and fired at GPMS over the week following class. Participants will need to return to GPMS to pick up their project about one week after class. Elena will contact you when items are ready to be picked up.\n\nGPMS will provide the clay\, glaze\, instruction\, and tools needed for this project.\n\nThis class costs $25 for non-members and $20 for members. If there is no one registered for class approximately 24 hours in advance\, class may be cancelled. Register here: GPMS Website\n\n\nTuesday\, October 13 | 6:30pm\nGreat Plains MakerSpace\, 2308 N 3rd St
URL:https://www.visitgck.com/event/gpms-class-clay-witch-hat-tea-lights/
LOCATION:Great Plains MakerSpace\, 2308 N. Third Street\, Garden City\, KS\, 67846\, United States
CATEGORIES:All Events
END:VEVENT
